DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:Connecticut: CT-1065/CT-1120SI due
DESCRIPTION:Connecticut partnership/S-corp composite return due the 15th da
 y of the 3rd month after year-end. Connecticut's PE Tax (elective as of 202
 4) is reported on this same return series. Correction (this rebuild session
 ): the cited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) wit
 hout addressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is 
 a Sunday. Consistent with every other state in this data set that explicitl
 y confirms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\
 , Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, an
 d with the near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to 
 the next business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshif
 ted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of t
 he general shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state con
 firmation that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for tran
 sparency. | Connecticut partnership/S-corp composite return due the 15th da
 y of the 3rd month after year-end. Connecticut's PE Tax (elective as of 202
 4) is reported on this same return series. File Form CT-1065/CT-1120SI EXT 
 for an automatic 6-month extension. Correction (this rebuild session): the 
 cited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without ad
 dressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunda
 y. Consistent with every other state in this data set that explicitly confi
 rms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaw
 are\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with 
 the near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the nex
 t business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted Mar
 ch 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the gene
 ral shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmati
 on that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparenc
 y. | Authority: Connecticut Department of Revenue Services\, direct fetch t
 his session: "on or before the fifteenth day of the third month following t
 he close of the taxable year"\; extension form confirms "a six-month extens
 ion of time to file Form CT-1065/CT-1120SI." | Source: https://portal.ct.go
 v/drs/taxes/pass-through-entity/tax-information | This date is computed fro
 m a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm 
 against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
