DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:Alabama: Form 65 due
DESCRIPTION:Alabama partnership/limited liability entity return due the 15t
 h day of the 3rd month after year-end (i.e. March 15 for calendar year). AL
  has an Electing Pass-Through Entity Tax (Form PTE-C) as a separate electio
 n. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states the general r
 ule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-specific weeken
 d interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with every other st
 ate in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. 
 Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all confir
 m shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US government-
 deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, this entry's dat
 e_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. 
 This is a computed application of the general shift convention\, not an ind
 ependently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specific state's sta
 tute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Alabama partnership/limited 
 liability entity return due the 15th day of the 3rd month after year-end (i
 .e. March 15 for calendar year). AL has an Electing Pass-Through Entity Tax
  (Form PTE-C) as a separate election. Federal extension automatically recog
 nized for Alabama purposes\; no separate AL extension form needed. Correcti
 on (this rebuild session): the cited source states the general rule (15th d
 ay of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-specific weekend interacti
 on - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with every other state in this
  data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachuset
 ts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting 
 to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US government-deadline co
 nvention of shifting to the next business day\, this entry's date_2026 was 
 corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a c
 omputed application of the general shift convention\, not an independently 
 re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specific state's statute shifts
  - flagged here for transparency. | Authority: Alabama Department of Revenu
 e\, direct fetch this session: "Returns made on the basis of calendar year 
 shall be filed on or before the 15th day of March following the close of th
 e calendar year" and "An extension of time to file an income tax return all
 owed for federal income tax purposes will be recognized for Alabama purpose
 s." | Source: https://www.revenue.alabama.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/23
 f65instr.pdf | This date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not ref
 lect a later-announced change\; confirm against the cited source before rel
